{#
  Rendered by roles/kustomize_apply from someguy_running_instances
  (roles/someguy/defaults/main.yml): one PersistentVolumeClaim per running
  instance, mounted at /data/someguy by its Deployment.

  One per instance. It holds the autoconf cache and the cached address book
  snapshot (cached-addr-book.ndjson); losing one costs only that instance's
  warm-up, which the other three absorb. ReadWriteOnce is safe because each
  Deployment is Recreate: the old pod is stopped before the new one mounts the
  same claim, so two pods never share it.
  1Gi documents intent, not a bound: local-path is hostPath-backed and does
  not enforce the request. The real bounds are someguy's PeerCacheSize (a
  26k-peer snapshot is about 6 MiB, ~250 MiB at the 1,000,000-peer cap) and
  the NVMe behind default-local-storage-path.
#}
{% for instance in someguy_running_instances %}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: {{ instance.name }}-data
spec:
  storageClassName: local-path
  accessModes: [ReadWriteOnce]
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi
{% endfor %}
